 record runs from 1951 to 2025, 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids. September to October came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2025, August to September ran 75% of normal on the middle of the grids, while April to May hit 132%. So far in 2026, January to February came in at 46% and May to June at 127% on the middle of the grids.</p>"}
